            "paragraph": "In addition, taking into account how COVID-19 has affected gender inequality, the pandemic has exacerbated pre-existing disparities in the Fragile Five countries, especially for women in economic and social spheres. Women, disproportionately represented in frontline healthcare and informal employment, faced higher risks of job loss and exposure to the virus. Lockdowns and school closures significantly increased unpaid care work, while restricted mobility contributed to a rise in domestic violence. These factors collectively intensified existing gender gaps, emphasizing the importance of considering pandemic-related effects when analyzing the interaction between climate change and gender inequality (UN Women, 2020).",
